; Explosions. The same simulation with a different source: instead of a fuel bed that burns
; steadily, a sphere of fuel and heat is thrown into the grid over the first hundredth of a
; second and the whole thing lives a couple of seconds. Names listed here are drawn as a
; fireball; the flash, the shock distortion and the flying debris stay the sprites they were.

; [shader_blast] maps a single effect. Use it only for one that nothing but an explosion ever
; plays: the sprites inside an explosion group are also played on their own elsewhere in the
; world, and hooking one of those sets off a fireball where nothing exploded.
[shader_blast]

; [shader_blast_group] is the safe form: the whole group gets a fireball of its own, and the
; sprites listed in [shader_blast_mute] are silenced inside those groups alone. The flash, the
; shock distortion and the flying debris are not listed, so they still play.
[shader_blast_group]
explosions\explosion_barrel = barrel
explosions\expl_mushroom_01 = barrel
explosions\expl_vehichels   = barrel

[shader_blast_mute]
explosions\effects\expl_benzin_05              = 1
explosions\effects\expl_benzin_veh             = 1
explosions\effects\expl_mushroom_glow00_barrel = 1

; blast_radius    the sphere the charge is injected into, m
; blast_lift      its centre above the effect origin, m
; blast_duration  how long the effect lives, s
; blast_inject    how long the charge keeps going in, s
; blast_speed     outward speed of the injected gas, m/s
; blast_pilot     the temperature the charge starts at
; blast_cell      one cell, m (0.09 = a 5.76 x 8.64 x 5.76 m box)

